course: dictionary
lesson: 6635
title: Now: one small word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Now» usually means at this time, at the present moment. In «How many cards does Ben have now?», now means the number after all the changes. In «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now», now means these days, as things stand.
explain: Now can also mean at once. In «Come here now!», the speaker wants action straight away. Now can start a sentence too, as in «Now, let's begin», where it means it is time to move on.
explain: «Now that» means because at this time. In «Now that it's sunny, let's go out», the sunshine is the reason. To check your meaning, swap in because and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Now means at this time or at the present moment.
fact: Now means at once, straight away, as in «Come here now!»
fact: «For now» means for the time being, and «by now» means already.
fact: «Now that» means because at this time.
fact: In texts, «rn» means right now, and «now you're talking» means that's a good idea.
exercise: «Most goods now cross the sea in standard steel boxes.» What does now mean here? | *At this time, these days | Because it is sunny | Immediately, at once | Long ago
exercise: «Now that it's sunny, let's go out.» What does now that mean? | Even though it is raining | Before it gets sunny | *Because it is sunny at this time | Never
exercise: «Come here now!» What does now mean? | For some days | *At once, straight away | Slowly | At this time next year
test: «He has been missing for some days now.» What does now mean here? | Yesterday | *Up to this present time | Immediately, at once | Because of the weather
test: Ella reads «rn» in a text from her friend. What does it mean? | Rough night | Really nice | *Right now | Read next
exam: Which word could replace now in «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now» in the exam voice? | for some days | *at present | at once | now that
